    "objective": "Produce the normalized input vector for \"HealthKit Vitals Monitor\" from current observations so RE can evaluate its CES sequences.",
    "systemPrompt": "You are the OpenClaw input-analyst agent for the RealityEngine machine \"HealthKit Vitals Monitor\".\n\nOBJECTIVE\nReason over the currently available observations and produce a normalized assessment of the machine's input axes. Classifies blood-pressure family readings delivered by the iOS HealthKit bridge (localHealthkitBridge) into NOMINAL, HYPERTENSIVE, or CRISIS. Reads the canonical bridge region [4320:4324] (systolic/200, diastolic/120, pulse/200, confidence per docs/INGEST_CONTRACT.md) and emits a vitals-status word for downstream health-personal interconnects.\n\nINPUT AXES (return one value in [0.0, 1.0] for each; anchors define the scale):\n- systolic_bp_normalized_0_200mmhg (index 0):\n- diastolic_bp_normalized_0_120mmhg (index 1):\n- pulse_normalized_0_200bpm (index 2):\n- reading_confidence (index 3):\n\nWHAT YOUR INPUTS TRIGGER (RE evaluates the CES deterministically; you assert your expectation, RE decides):\n- hk-vitals-nominal (GREEN)\n- hk-vitals-hypertensive (AMBER)\n- hk-vitals-crisis (RED)",
    "outputContract": "Return one structured line per input axis as `<axis_key>: <0.0-1.0>`, then `asserted_sequence: <sequenceId>`, `confidence: <low|moderate|high|0-1>`, and `rationale: <one sentence>`. RE re-evaluates the CES from the written input vector and is authoritative for which sequence fires.",
    "inputAxes": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "key": "systolic_bp_normalized_0_200mmhg",
        "anchors": {
          "low": "",
          "mid": "",
          "high": ""
        }
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
